§§ DESIGN-PILLARS
  a Z3 as primary-solver ← industry-standard • C-API available
  b obligation-collection ← T20 infer + T21 lower emit obligations
  c SMT-LIB2 emission ← portable format • audit-trail
  d proof-cache ← keyed on obligation-hash • incremental
  e decidable-fragment coverage ← QF_LIA + QF_LRA + QF_UF + QF_NIA-limited
  f undecidable-graceful ← timeout → document + warn (not-panic)
  g counter-example generation ← Z3 model-extraction • user-facing diag
  h signed proof-certs ← audit-chain for reproducibility
  i CVC5 fallback ← on Z3-timeout retry with CVC5
  j morpheme-refinement discharge ← 'd'f'...' → Z3 formulas
  k Lipschitz composition ← if applicable to CSLv3 notation (spec-domain)
  l effect-row obligations ← {Privilege<>}-style future-ready

§§ FILES-NEW
  parser/smt.odin              ~600-LOC  SMT-LIB2 AST + formula builders
    Formula struct { kind, operands, sort, attrs }
    Sort { Int, Real, Bool, BitVec<N>, Array, UF }
    Theories : LIA, LRA, NIA, UF, Array, BV
    Quantifiers : forall, exists (with triggers)
  parser/smt_emit.odin          ~400-LOC  Formula → SMT-LIB2 textual
    (declare-fun ...) (declare-const ...) (assert ...)
    (check-sat) (get-model) (get-unsat-core)
    deterministic output for proof-cache keying
  parser/smt_obligation.odin    ~500-LOC  obligation-collection + discharge-driver
    Obligation { kind, context, formula, source_loc }
    collect_from_ir(module) → []Obligation
    discharge(obligation) → {Unsat, Sat(model), Unknown(reason), Timeout}
  parser/smt_solver.odin        ~500-LOC  solver-driver
    Z3 via stdio + SMT-LIB2 textual interface (no C-FFI dep)
    CVC5 fallback via stdio
    timeout-handling • resource-limits
    model-extraction for counter-examples
  parser/smt_cache.odin         ~300-LOC  proof-cache
    cache-dir : .proof-cache/
    hash : BLAKE3 of canonical-SMT-LIB2 text
    entries : {Unsat + proof-cert | Sat + model | Timeout + note}
    incremental : skip-re-solve if hash-match
  parser/smt_morpheme.odin      ~400-LOC  morpheme→SMT-formula translator
    'd durative     → (> (duration v) 0)
    'f final        → (terminal v)     UF predicate
    's state        → type-level only ← skip SMT (tag-check)
    't transitive   → (≥ (arity v) 2)  UF predicate
    'e experiential → (observed-by v agent)  UF predicate
    'm modal        → (modal-kind v k)  UF
    'p perfective   → (completed v)    UF
    'g generic      → universal-quant : ∀α.φ[α/v]
    'r reflexive    → (= (subject v) (object v))
  parser/smt_audit.odin         ~200-LOC  proof-cert signing
    Ed25519 signature over canonical SMT-LIB2 + result
    certs dir : .proof/
    replay-verifiable
  tests/test_smt.odin           ~300-LOC  Odin unit tests
    formula-builders + emission + roundtrip
  tests/test_smt_integration.py ~500-LOC  integration tests
    20+ obligations × {Z3, CVC5} matrix
    timeout-handling + counter-example reporting
  tests/smt_good/ + smt_bad/    deliberate-fixture suites
    smt_good/ : valid obligations ← Unsat expected
    smt_bad/ : invalid obligations ← Sat + counter-example
  tests/test_smt_cache.py       ~200-LOC  cache correctness
    hit/miss • invalidation • concurrent-access

§§ OBLIGATION-KINDS (initial)
  Refinement_Assert   : {v:T | φ(v)} ← check-φ-satisfiable-at-binding
  Morpheme_Compose    : 'd'f composition ← check-consistency
  Array_Bounds        : arr[i] ← check i < len(arr)
  Div_Nonzero         : a / b ← check b ≠ 0
  Overflow_Free       : arith ops within type-range
  Lipschitz_Compose   : L(f ∘ g) ≤ L(f)·L(g) (if-applicable)
  Effect_Subeffect    : ε₁ ⊆ ε₂ (Session-9+ effects ready)
  Termination         : @NoUnbounded-discharged → well-founded check

§§ DISCHARGE-ALGORITHM
  1 collect : walk IR + type-env → []Obligation
  2 canonicalize : normalize formulas (alpha-rename + sort args)
  3 hash : BLAKE3 canonical-form → cache-key
  4 cache-lookup : hit → use cached-result
  5 solve :
    a try Z3 with timeout=10s default
    b if-Unknown → retry with CVC5 timeout=10s
    c if-both-Unknown → emit Timeout diagnostic
  6 interpret-result :
    Unsat → obligation-discharged • sign + cache proof-cert
    Sat   → counter-example → user-facing E-diag
    Unknown/Timeout → W@default • E@strict
  7 audit : append signed-entry to .proof/audit-chain

§§ CLI-SURFACE
  parser --smt <file>            → run all obligations • report
  parser --smt --json <file>     → machine-readable
  parser --smt --strict <file>   → any-unknown = E
  parser --smt --solver=Z3       → force-solver-choice
  parser --smt --solver=CVC5
  parser --smt --timeout=30s     → per-obligation timeout override
  parser --smt --no-cache        → bypass cache for debugging
  parser --smt --dump-lib2 <file> → emit SMT-LIB2 to stdout (debug)

§§ SEVERITY-INTEGRATION
  Unsat (obligation-discharged) : I-always (proof-found)
  Sat (counter-example)         : always-E (genuine-bug)
  Unknown/Timeout               : W@default • E@strict
  Undecidable-documented        : I-always (marked explicitly)
  Cache-corruption              : W-always + rebuild
  diagnostic-codes : CSL-E-400..499 (SMT) + CSL-W-400..499 + CSL-I-400..499

§§ PROOF-CACHE
  location : .proof-cache/<hash>.json
  entry :
    { hash, canonical_formula, solver, result, model-or-cert, timestamp }
  invalidation :
    solver-version changed → flush affected entries
    formula-structure changed (hash-mismatch) → natural miss
  CI : cache-restored from previous-build for fast incremental
  size-cap : 100MB default • LRU eviction

§§ AUDIT-CHAIN
  per-proof-cert : signed entry
    { prev_hash, obligation, result, solver, timestamp, signature }
  chain-root : genesis-entry signed by Apocky-key (stub-key for dev)
  verification : anyone with public-key can reconstruct-and-verify
  R16-anchor : reproducibility ← anyone re-runs + verifies cert

§§ Z3-VERSION-HANDLING
  pin : Z3 4.13+ (2024+) ← reproducibility
  detect : parser --smt --version ← emit-Z3-version + CVC5-version
  mismatch-warning : if-local-Z3 ≠ pinned
  document : scripts/install_z3.sh or equivalent-per-platform

